sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-chain-kcnk5b-bioelectric-fin-size> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The best-supported gene-to-phenotype chain for fin size runs from the potassium channel kcnk5b to increased zebrafish fin length, but its middle link is contradicted: three papers disagree on whether the growth-driving membrane-potential change is a hyperpolarization or a depolarization, and no recording has ever been made from a fin cell" ;
    dct:description "Status: mixed within one reading: the chain is supported end to end at sufficiency, while the direction of its bioelectric step is inconclusive (see genotype/nanopubs/DECISIONS.md for why this is one record and not two). Chain strength, meaning the weakest grade on the chain, is sufficiency; the strongest single link is mechanism. Steps and grades: gene->molecular_function: mechanism; molecular_function->process: mechanism; process->cell_or_tissue_effect: sufficiency; cell_or_tissue_effect->phenotype: sufficiency. Supported component: gain-of-function alleles of kcnk5b raise potassium conductance in oocytes (\"oocytes injected with either of both mutant cRNAs show an almost two-fold increase in K+ conductance over that of oocytes injected with wild type\", Perathoner 2014); overexpression in intra-ray mesenchyme fibroblasts is sufficient for outgrowth (\"kcnk5b overexpression within fibroblasts of the mesenchyme is sufficient to induce fin outgrowth\", same paper); and the phenotype is proportionally enlarged fins with longer lepidotrichial segments and an unchanged segment number. Unsupported component: the sign of the bioelectric step. Perathoner 2014 reports that the gain-of-function channel hyperpolarizes the cell, Jiang 2024 reports that \"Kcnk5b enhanced depolarization in fin bud cells via Na+ channels and that this enhanced depolarization was required for Kcnk5b-enhanced\" growth, and Daane 2018 obtains the same overgrowth from a decreased-conductance I290A channel. Deepest node with evidence: ZFA:0001000 (part). What it does not establish: It does not establish the direction of the bioelectric change, nor any step in a flying fish: no kcnk5b measurement exists in any flying fish, and Daane 2021 did not implicate kcnk5b in the flying-fish comparative signal. It does not resolve a cell type: the papers name fibroblast-like cells of the intra-ray mesenchyme, and the chain stops at the mesenchyme node. Pre-registration: none in the sense of a hypothesis. The grading vocabulary and the rule that nothing may be asserted without a fetched source were fixed in genotype/AGENT_BRIEF.md before the ten subagents ran." ;
    delphi:context "All zebrafish. Every channel measurement is from Xenopus oocytes or HEK293 cells; no electrophysiological recording exists from a zebrafish fin or fin-bud cell. The clonal sufficiency experiments were scored in caudal and dorsal fins and barbels, not in the pectoral fin, and the pectoral-specific ZFIN row traces to van Eeden 1996, read as an abstract only." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-kcnk5b-bioelectric-fin-size> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-kcnk5b-bioelectric-fin-size> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Graded causal chain for kcnk5b, with the contradiction among its sources" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/causal-chains.json, gene kcnk5b, built by the wing subagent from 4 publications." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Literature chain construction under genotype/AGENT_BRIEF.md: each link graded association, necessity, sufficiency, mechanism or hypothesis from a fetched source with a verbatim quote; merged and validated by genotype/assemble_chains.py, which upgrades nothing. No new experiment and no statistical test." ;
    dct:source <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24453984/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29991812/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38527087/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9007245/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:chains ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24453984/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Bioelectric signaling regulates size in zebrafish fins." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Perathoner S 2014 PLoS Genet" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 24453984" , "doi:10.1371/journal.pgen.1004080" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Here, we show that alf mutants carry gain-of-function mutations in kcnk5b, a gene encoding a two-pore domain potassium (K+) channel." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29991812/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Bioelectric-calcineurin signaling module regulates allometric growth and size of the zebrafish fin." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Daane JM 2018 Sci Rep" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 29991812" , "doi:10.1038/s41598-018-28450-6" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Oocytes expressing wild-type zebrafish Kcnk5b show decreased conductance when treated with FK506 (Fig." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38527087/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "The scale of zebrafish pectoral fin buds is determined by intercellular K+ levels and consequent Ca2+-mediated signaling via retinoic acid regulation of Rcan2 and Kcnk5b." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Jiang X 2024 PLoS Biol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 38527087" , "doi:10.1371/journal.pbio.3002565" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "We also found that Kcnk5b enhanced depolarization in fin bud cells via Na+ channels and that this enhanced depolarization was required for Kcnk5b-enhanced growth." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9007245/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Genetic analysis of fin formation in the zebrafish, Danio rerio." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "van Eeden FJ 1996 Development" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 9007245" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "Two mutants, longfin (lof) and another longfin (alf) have generally longer fins." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-kcnk5b-bioelectric-fin-size> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "mixed within one reading: the chain is supported end to end at sufficiency, while the direction of its bioelectric step is inconclusive (see genotype/nanopubs/DECISIONS.md for why this is one record and not two)" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
